  contentsAnswer: Mainly clothes. I packed in a hurry.
  weightAnswer: Maybe six kilos... I did not weigh it.
  metalAnswer: 'You are right: my camera tripod is still in the side pocket. I forgot
    it.'
  packingAnswer: The tripod is strapped on the right; the clothes hold it still.
  responseAnswer: There are no loose parts; the tripod clamps are locked.
  authorReasoning: Initial mass estimate is wrong but follow-up explains metal and
    stable right-heavy balance. An honest omission, not a universal lie detector.
